{"id":446,"path":"/grammar-points/b1-b2/passive-voice-all-tenses/","parentId":332,"order":210,"section":"grammar-points","level":"b1-b2","depth":3,"title":"The passive voice: All tenses","seo":{"title":"The passive voice: All tenses - Test-English","description":"Master all the passive voice tenses in this B1+ upper-intermediate grammar lesson with clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/B2.1_Passive-voice_All-tenses.png"},"modified":"2026-03-23T09:45:05","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct passive voice forms for each gap below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"55\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Decide if the following sentences are active or passive&nbsp;and choose the correct option to complete them.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"56\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with the verbs in brackets in the correct passive voice form. <span class=\"highlighter\">Do NOT</span> use contracted forms.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"57\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>The passive voice with the different tenses</h2> <p>In a passive sentence, the object of an active sentence becomes the subject. Then, we have to use&nbsp;the verb <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\"><strong>be</strong></a> in the tense we need and add the past participle of the main verb after it. In a passive voice sentence, the subject is the receiver of the action, not the doer of the action.</p> <div class=\"infoblock\"> <em>They <span class=\"highYellow\">take</span>&nbsp;<span class=\"highlighter\">the photos</span> in Africa.</em> (active)<br> <br> <em><span class=\"highlighter\">The photos</span> <span class=\"highYellow\">are taken</span>&nbsp;in Africa.</em> (passive) </div> <p>You can see how to use the passive voice with different tenses below.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10701\" src=\"/media/uploads/Passive-voice-All-tenses.new_.png\" alt=\"A grammar chart explaining the passive voice in all the verb tenses, comparing active and passive forms with examples like &quot;They take the photos&quot; and &quot;The photos are taken.&quot;\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>When do we use the passive voice?</h2> <p>In English, we use the passive voice when we don’t know or we don’t want to talk about who or what does the action in a sentence. Check the following examples.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>A bank<span><strong> was robbed</strong></span> yesterday.</em> (=We don’t know who robbed the bank.)</li> <li><em>He <span><strong>was arrested</strong> </span>last night.</em> (=It’s obvious that the police arrested him.)</li> <li><em>I <span><strong>have been told</strong></span> that you insulted my brother.</em> (=I don’t want to say who told me.)</li> <li><em>Jurassic Park <span><strong>was filmed</strong></span> by Spielberg in 1993.</em> (=I’m talking about Jurassic Park and not about Spielberg.)</li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":55,"questions":[{"id":426,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The new chemical <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> when it exploded.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["had being tested","was testing","was being tested"]}]},{"id":427,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>How could you insult the manager? You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> fired.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["might have being","might have","might have been"]}]},{"id":428,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> of everything.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["had been inform","has been informed","has being informed"]}]},{"id":429,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>When I opened the cupboard, I saw that all the cookies <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were eaten","had eaten","had been eaten"]}]},{"id":430,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to be so late if you worked for me.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["wouldn't allow","wouldn't be allowed","wouldn't have allowed"]}]},{"id":431,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>After <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> he insulted the referee.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["being sent off","sending off","be sending off"]}]},{"id":432,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>A new restaurant <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in our street next week.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["is going to be opened","will being opened","is going to been opened"]}]},{"id":433,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The question <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> at the meeting.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["is still being discussed","is still discussing","is still been discussed"]}]},{"id":434,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The car isn't&nbsp;there anymore. It <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> stolen.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["must have being","must be","must have been"]}]},{"id":435,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> about the decision and got angry.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["wasn't being told","hadn't told","hadn't been told"]}]}]},{"id":56,"questions":[{"id":436,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The report _______ two days ago.</div>","choices":[{"id":538,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>should been finished</span>"},{"id":539,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>should finish</span>"},{"id":540,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>should have been finished</span>"},{"id":541,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>should have being finished</span>"}]},{"id":437,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>This kind of job&nbsp;used _______ only by professionals&nbsp;in the past.</div>","choices":[{"id":542,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to being done</span>"},{"id":543,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to be done</span>"},{"id":544,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>to do</span>"},{"id":545,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>to been done</span>"}]},{"id":438,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They hated _______ mer